# Overview

Controllers in Amber are similar to Rails but have some key differences.

One of these differences is the organization into folders.

the `src/controllers/` folder is the main starting point. There are 3 main folders that controllers get grouped into:

1. `public` - this is for any controller that doesn't require authentication for a persona
2. `authenicated` - this for any controller that handles an authentication restricted resource and which renders a view back to the requester
3. `api` - this is for requests being processed that will not have a standard view rendered back for them. This may or may not have authenticated controllers, in most cases these controllers will have routes/actions that are protected by authentication.
4. Each of these folders has it's own "base" controller that sets the default before/after calls and helper methods that will get used throughout it's child controllers.

# Naming Conventions

Each controller in the folder is namespaced to reflect that folder, with the controller name being the last part.

For example:

An API controller about a resource named "Address" would be: `Api::AddressController < Api::BaseApiController`
